# Tutorial: Custom Cryptographic Tool Development

## 1. Setting Up the Project

Create a new folder named `crypto_tool` and open it in your IDE.

```
cd crypto_tool
mkdir crypto_tool
cd crypto_tool
```

Inside, create a `.cs` file with the following structure:

```
[System.Serializable]
public class CryptoTool
{
    public string Name { get; set; }
    public string Description { get; set; }
    public int Version { get; set; }
    public string Author { get; set; }
}
```

## 2. Defining the Tool Interface

In `CryptoTool.cs`, implement the `ICryptoTool` interface.

```csharp
public interface ICryptoTool
{
    void Encrypt(string input, string output);
    void Decrypt(string input, string output);
    void ProcessIncome(string input, string output);
}
```

